B.Wf=new A.hN(3,"Temperature and Ventilation Control","Step-down cooling, fresh air, and ammonia removal","1 min read",B.atK,"Good air & temperature cuts feed waste by up to 15% and prevents heat stress.","Target brooding temperatures:\n\n\u2022 Days 1-3: 33-34\xb0C\n\u2022 Days 4-7: 32\xb0C\n\u2022 Week 2: 29\xb0C\n\u2022 Week 3: 27\xb0C\n\u2022 Week 4+: 22-24\xb0C\n\nVentilation is vital: insufficient fresh air causes ammonia buildup and ascites (water belly).",u.c,"What is the primary risk of improper ventilation in the barn?",B.aco,1,"Poor air exchange traps ammonia and carbon dioxide, damaging the respiratory tract and causing ascites (water belly) in fast-growing broilers.")
