B.Wr=new A.hN(5,"Diseases and Working with Veterinarians","Entry disinfection, >1% red alert, and safe vet care","1 min read",B.agW,"Prevention costs pennies compared to treatment and protects your entire loan repayment.","The golden rule of poultry farming: prevention is vastly cheaper than treatment!\n\n\u2022 Strict biosecurity: disinfection mats at entrances, designated footwear.\n\u2022 If daily mortality exceeds 1%, immediately isolate the barn and call a veterinarian.\n\u2022 Never administer antibiotics without professional prescription.",u.q,"What emergency action should be taken if daily mortality exceeds 1%?",B.adH,1,"Daily mortality above 1% is a critical red alert indicating potential infectious outbreak or acute climate failure; immediate veterinary intervention is mandatory.")
